  "_tenantColumns_comment": "Sparse override of the project column each source table's row filter is applied to, keyed by table. Only tables whose column is not the default 'TenantId' appear (e.g. stored_objects carries 'project_id'). Derived from the application catalog's LangWatchQLViewDefinition.tenantColumn and asserted equal by manifestParity.unit.test.ts. An absent table, an absent map, and an empty value all render 'TenantId', so an older manifest is unchanged.",
  "tenantColumns": {
    "stored_objects": "project_id"
  },
  "_sourceColumns_comment": "The exact columns the langwatch_lwql user is granted SELECT on for each source table, keyed by table \u2014 mirroring the app's column-scoped grants (catalogStatements.ts lwqlSourceColumnGrants) so the chart-rendered SaaS role reads only the columns the catalog exposes, not every column of the fact table. Asserted equal to the catalog by platform/app/src/server/analytics/lwql/catalog/__tests__/manifestParity.unit.test.ts. Sparse: a source absent here (the PostgreSQL-engine *_pg bridge tables, whose whole column list is the exposed surface) takes the whole-object GRANT SELECT.",
